# The non-C++ linters for ci.yml's script-lint job (roadmap VX14): ruff over
# every Python file in the tree, shellcheck over the shell scripts, actionlint
# over the workflows.
#
# shellcheck and actionlint are Haskell and Go programs, not Python ones -
# these two PyPI packages are the upstream-blessed wrappers that ship the
# real, unmodified binary inside a wheel (the same route pre-commit uses).
# Going through pip for all three is what lets the whole gate hash-pin in one
# lock here, exactly like requirements-coverage.txt and
# requirements-ffmpeg-validate.txt, instead of curl-ing two release tarballs
# and hand-maintaining their checksums in the workflow.
#
# All three are dependency-free binary wrappers, so this lock carries no
# environment markers and installs the same way on any Python the runner
# image ships.
#
# Regenerate the lock after any change here with:
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#     --output-file=requirements-lint.txt requirements-lint.in
ruff
shellcheck-py
actionlint-py
